swering its own questions.[6;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m 5 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//(B[m[38;2;192;202;245m[10X[7;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m 6 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m// A program asks its terminal things on startup —[7;57H "what are you" (DA), "are[8;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m 7 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m// you there" (DSR), "do you support synchronized output" (DECRQM). Until now[9;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m 8 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m// the ANSWERS came from xterm.js in the browser, which has two consequences[10;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m 9 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m// rook keeps paying for:[11;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m10 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//(B[m[38;2;192;202;245m[53X[12;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m11 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//  1. Nobody answers a detached session. readPump runs whether or not a[13;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m12 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//     client is attached, but the replies do not —[13;58H so a program started in a[14;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m13 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//     background workspace blocks on a DA1 that never comes. Harmless today[15;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m14 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//     only because rook attaches everything; the detach work removes that.[16;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m15 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//(B[m[38;2;192;202;245m [17;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m16 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//  2. A reattaching client re-parses the whole replayed ring and answers[18;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m17 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//     every query in it a second time, to a program that asked once and long[19;5H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m8 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//     since moved on. That is a whole subsystem in term/manager.ts —[19;76H a gate,[20;5H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m9 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//     a timer, a marker frame, and a regex —[20;52H and the $y hole in that regex is[21;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m20 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//     what put five stale mode reports into a live nvim.(B[m[38;2;192;202;245m[7X[22;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m21 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//(B[m[38;2;192;202;245m[35X[23;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m22 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m// Both dissolve if the host answers. It sees every byte the program writes,[24;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m23 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m// it is always there, and its reply goes in as INPUT so it never lands in the[25;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m24 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m// ring to be replayed at all.[26;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m25 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//(B[m[38;2;192;202;245m[3X[27;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m26 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m// What the host CANNOT answer is the honest boundary of this idea, and worth[28;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m27 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m// stating because it is the same boundary a server-side emulator would move:[29;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m28 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//[30;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m29 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//   CPR (CSI 6 n)      needs the cursor position[31;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m30 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//   DECRQSS (DCS $ q)  needs the current SGR/cursor state[32;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m31 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//   OSC 4/10-12        needs the palette, which lives in the theme[33;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m32 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//(B[m[38;2;192;202;245m[15X[34;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m33 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m// Each needs a model of the screen rather than a model of the conversation.[35;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m34 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m// Those stay with xterm.js, and term/manager.ts still filters them during[36;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m35 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m// replay. Everything below is answerable from the byte stream alone.[37;4H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m36 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m//(B[m[38;2;192;202;245m[8X[38;3H(B[m[38;2;59;66;97m 37 (B[m[3m[38;2;86;95;137m// The answers mirror xterm.js's exactly (InputHandler.requestMode), including(B[m[38;2;192;202;245m[